{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And of Asher he said: Blessed be Asher above sons.</b> Since regarding his wife it is written (Genesis 30:13): ״בְּאָשְׁרִי כִּי אִשְּׁרוּנִי בָּנוֹת״ — for the daughters blessed him — therefore he added to say that he would also be blessed and happy from sons, for both son and daughter, all of them, would call him happy and bless him." "And as for what is said, <b>and as your days, so your old age</b> — this alludes to the saying of our Sages of blessed memory (Ḥullin 24a): 'The oil with which my mother anointed me in my youth is what sustained me in my old age.' Therefore he said here: ״וְטֹבֵל בַּשֶּׁמֶן רַגְלוֹ״, and by means of the oil he would be strong and healthy in the days of old age as in his youth; this is what it says: ״וּכְיָמֶיךָ דָּבְאֶךָ״. And according to the opinion of those who say that Asher was blessed with many children through fulfilling the commandment of procreation in his youth and in his old age, as it is written (Ecclesiastes 11:6): ״בַּבֹּקֶר זְרַע אֶת זַרְעֶךָ וְלָעֶרֶב״ etc., this is what it says ״וּכְיָמֶיךָ דָּבְאֶךָ״, as Rashi explained, that it comes to equate the days of old age with the days of youth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:48.477701529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}